  background:var(--cream-light);
  border:1px solid rgba(61,92,93,.12);
  border-radius:20px;
  padding:24px;
}
.fit-card p{
  font-size:14px;
  color:var(--stone);
}
.cta-shell{
  margin-top:32px;
  background:linear-gradient(166deg,var(--brand-darker) 6%, var(--brand-dark) 94%);
  color:var(--white);
  border-radius:28px;
  padding:34px 30px;
  box-shadow:0 20px 42px rgba(45,70,71,.18);
}
.cta-shell .eyebrow{
  color:var(--gold-light);
}
.cta-shell h2{
  color:var(--white);
  margin-top:10px;
  font-size:clamp(24px,4vw,40px);
  line-height:1.08;
}
.cta-shell > p{
  color:rgba(255,255,255,.88);
  max-width:760px;
  margin-top:12px;
}
.cta-button{
  margin-top:24px;
}
.cta-note{
  margin-top:16px;
  font-size:13px !important;
  line-height:1.55 !important;
  color:var(--gold-light) !important;
  max-width:760px;
}
.method-mobile{
  display:none;
}
.footer{
  text-align:center;
  color:var(--stone-light);
  font-size:14px;
  padding:0 24px 42px;
}
@media (max-width:980px){
  .hero,
  .compare-grid,
  .fit-grid{
    grid-template-columns:1fr;
  }
  .comparison-grid{
    grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));
  }
  .layer-grid{
    grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));
  }
  .example-grid{
    grid-template-columns:1fr;
  }
}
@media (max-width:720px){
  .desktop-only{display:none !important}
  .mobile-only{display:block !important}
  .guide-nav{padding:12px 16px}
  .page{padding:84px 16px 48px}
  .hero,
  .section,
  .cta-shell{padding:20px}
  .hero{
    grid-template-columns:1fr;
    gap:12px;
    border-radius:24px;
  }
  .hero h1{
    font-size:38px;
    line-height:1.05;
    max-width:8ch;
  }
  .hero-lead{
    font-size:15px;
    line-height:1.6;
  }
  .hero-caption{
    display:block;
  }
  .comparison-grid,
  .compare-grid,
  .scenario-table-wrap{
    display:none;
  }
  .hero-mobile-scope{
    display:flex;
    margin-top:16px;
  }
  .hero-mobile-actions{
    display:grid;
    gap:10px;
    margin-top:10px;
  }
  .hero-mobile-actions .btn{
    width:100%;
  }
  .hero-mobile-actions .hero-secondary{
    width:max-content;
    color:var(--brand-dark);
    border-color:rgba(61,92,93,.32);
  }
  .compare-mobile,
  .scenario-cards{
    display:grid;
    gap:12px;
  }
  .layer-grid{
    grid-template-columns:1fr;
    padding:0;
    background:none;
    border:none;
    gap:12px;
  }
  .comparison-grid{
    display:grid;
    grid-template-columns:1fr;
    gap:12px;
  }
  .fit-grid{
    grid-template-columns:1fr;
  }
  .section-caption{
    font-size:12px;
  }
  .method-mobile{
    display:block;
  }
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<nav class="guide-nav">
  <a href="/research/">← Research</a>
  <span class="logo">Seascape Vacations</span>
</nav>

<main class="page">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <span class="eyebrow">Owner Fee + Revenue Leak Benchmark</span>
      <span class="scope-pill desktop-only">{{ benchmark.scopeLabel }}</span>
      <h1>Your management fee is not the whole revenue leak.</h1>
      <p class="hero-lead">Most owners compare 15%, 20%, and 25% management fees. That misses Airbnb fees, more direct bookings, rate control, and how clearly your manager explains what actually reaches your payout.</p>
      <p class="hero-support desktop-only"><strong>What actually reaches my owner statement?</strong> A lower management fee does not always mean a better result. <strong>Source note:</strong> Observed Seascape portfolio data is labeled separately from scenario math and property examples.</p>
      <p class="hero-caption mobile-only">This benchmark is a decision aid, not a revenue forecast or market-wide fee survey.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions desktop-only">
        <a class="btn btn-gold" href="{{ ctaPath }}" data-track-event="owner_primary_cta_click" data-page-slug="owner-fee-revenue-leak-benchmark-2026">Request Your Revenue Teardown</a>
        <a class="hero-secondary" href="#benchmark-math">See the benchmark math</a>
      </div>
      <div class="proof-rail desktop-only">
        {% for label in proofLabels %}
        <span class="proof-chip">{{ label }}</span>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-side desktop-only">
      <div class="side-panel">
        <span class="eyebrow">Observed Seascape portfolio data</span>
        <h2 class="hero-stack-title">Fee stack quick read</h2>
        <p class="hero-stack-copy">The benchmark opens with the fee, booking-source cost, direct path, and reporting story together so you can see the pressure points in one place.</p>
        <div class="hero-stack-list">
          {% for row in heroStackRows %}
          <div class="hero-stack-row">
            <div class="hero-stack-text">
              <strong>{{ row.title }}</strong>
              <span>{{ row.detail }}</span>
            </div>
            <div class="hero-stack-track"><span class="hero-stack-fill" style="width:{{ row.width }}%;background:{{ row.fill }}"></span></div>
            <div class="hero-stack-value">{{ row.value }}</div>
          </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
        <p class="hero-stack-note">Compact visual only. The full comparison, scenario math, and proof notes continue below.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="side-panel">
        <span class="eyebrow">How To Read This</span>
        <ul class="method-list">
          {% for note in methodNotes %}
          <li>{{ note }}</li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="hero-mobile-scope mobile-only">
    <span class="proof-chip proof-chip--soft">{{ benchmark.scopeLabel }}</span>
  </div>

  <div class="hero-mobile-actions mobile-only">
    <a class="btn btn-gold" href="{{ ctaPath }}" data-track-event="owner_primary_cta_click" data-page-slug="owner-fee-revenue-leak-benchmark-2026">Request Your Revenue Teardown</a>
    <a class="hero-secondary" href="#benchmark-math">See the benchmark math</a>
  </div>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-intro">
      <span class="eyebrow">The wrong comparison</span>
      <h2>A lower management fee can still leave owner revenue exposed.</h2>
      <p>The headline fee matters, but it is not the whole picture. If most stays come through expensive booking paths, if rate control is soft, if cleaning-heavy subtotals push Airbnb fees higher, or if the reporting stays vague, you can still keep less even when the management fee looks competitive.</p>
      <p class="section-strong">That is why the real comparison is what actually reaches your owner statement.</p>
      <div class="section-proof-rail">
        <span class="proof-chip proof-chip--soft">Observed Seascape portfolio data</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="comparison-grid">
      {% for card in comparisonCards %}
      <article class="comparison-card">
        <span class="comparison-label">{{ card.label }}</span>
        <h3>{{ card.title }}</h3>
        <p>{{ card.copy }}</p>
      </article>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
    <p class="section-caption">This benchmark is a decision aid, not a revenue forecast or market-wide fee survey.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="benchmark-math">
    <div class="section-intro">
      <span class="eyebrow">Where the pressure shows up</span>
      <h2>What you keep changes in layers.</h2>
      <p>The management fee is only the first layer. Airbnb fees, direct payment cost, booking sources, rate softness, and weak reporting can all change the amount you actually keep. If you want the longer breakdown on owner income, pair this page with <a href="/property-management/maximize-vacation-rental-income-florida/">what lowers owner income on Gulf Coast homes</a>.</p>
      <div class="section-proof-rail">
        <span class="proof-chip proof-chip--soft">Observed Seascape portfolio data</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="layer-grid">
      {% for layer in feeLayers %}
      <article class="layer-card">
        <h3>{{ layer.title }}</h3>
        <p>{{ layer.copy }}</p>
      </article>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
    <p class="mini-note">Airbnb fees can apply to the full booking subtotal, including cleaning. That is why cleaning-heavy stays can carry a higher effective commission than owners expect.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-intro">
      <span class="eyebrow">Booking channels</span>
      <h2>Airbnb fees can move what you keep as much as the management fee.</h2>
      <p>In Seascape's current five-home benchmark, Airbnb host-fee cost averages 13.4% on post-October 2025 Seascape bookings. Direct payment cost is 2.9%. That gap is why booking sources belong in the conversation.</p>
      <div class="section-proof-rail">
        <span class="proof-chip proof-chip--soft">Observed Seascape portfolio data</span>
        <span class="proof-chip proof-chip--soft">{{ benchmark.refreshedLabel }}</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="compare-grid">
      <div class="compare-panel">
        <span class="eyebrow">Observed Seascape portfolio data</span>
        <h3>Airbnb cost vs direct payment cost</h3>
        <div class="bar-list">
          <div class="bar-row">
            <div class="bar-label">Airbnb booking</div>
            <div class="bar-track"><span class="bar-fill" style="width:89%;background:var(--gold)"></span></div>
            <div class="bar-value">13.4%</div>
          </div>
          <div class="bar-row">
            <div class="bar-label">Direct booking</div>
            <div class="bar-track"><span class="bar-fill" style="width:19%;background:var(--brand-dark)"></span></div>
            <div class="bar-value">2.9%</div>
          </div>
          <div class="bar-row">
            <div class="bar-label">Difference to review</div>
            <div class="bar-track"><span class="bar-fill" style="width:70%;background:rgba(95,138,139,.38)"></span></div>
            <div class="bar-value">10.5 pts</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="mini-note">Observed Seascape cost references. Airbnb fees are an observed Seascape average; direct cost is a payment reference. This chart is not a market-wide fee survey.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="compare-panel">
        <span class="eyebrow">What to check next</span>
        <ul class="quick-list">
          <li>Airbnb can take its cut on the full booking subtotal, including cleaning-heavy stays.</li>
          <li>A calendar can look busy while the booking path still leaves too much money behind.</li>
          <li>The point is not that direct solves everything. It is whether the current mix is more expensive than it needs to be.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="compare-mobile mobile-only">
      <article class="compare-mobile-card">
        <h3>Airbnb booking</h3>
        <strong>13.4% observed host-fee cost</strong>
        <p>Observed Seascape average, not a universal Airbnb claim.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="compare-mobile-card">
        <h3>Direct booking</h3>
        <strong>2.9% direct payment cost</strong>
        <p>Direct payment reference, not a promise that every stay can move direct.</p>
      </article>
      <p class="mini-note">Observed Seascape cost references. Airbnb fees are an observed Seascape average; direct cost is a payment reference. This chart is not a market-wide fee survey.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-intro">
      <span class="eyebrow">Sample comparison</span>
      <h2>The same management fee can still lead to different results.</h2>
      <p>Use this as a simple way to read the money story. The point is not to forecast a specific home. The point is to show why management fee, booking-source costs, and more direct bookings should be evaluated together.</p>
      <div class="section-proof-rail">
        <span class="proof-chip proof-chip--soft">Scenario math, not a forecast</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="scenario-table-wrap">
      <table class="scenario-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Scenario</th>
            <th>What changes</th>
            <th>What it means for your payout</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for row in scenarioRows %}
          <tr>
            <td>{{ row.title }}</td>
            <td>{{ row.change }}</td>
            <td>{{ row.implication }}</td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="scenario-cards mobile-only">
      {% for row in scenarioRows %}
      <article class="scenario-card">
        <h3>{{ row.title }}</h3>
        <p>{{ row.change }}</p>
        <p class="scenario-card-note">{{ row.implication }}</p>
      </article>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
    <p class="mini-note">Scenario math showing how booking-source costs can change what you keep. It is not a forecast, guarantee, or property-specific quote.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-intro">
      <span class="eyebrow">Observed Seascape examples</span>
      <h2>Three examples from the current benchmark inputs.</h2>
      <p>These examples are narrow on purpose. They show what Seascape has observed in its own operating data, not what every Gulf Coast home should expect.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="example-grid">
      {% for example in benchmark.examples %}
      <article class="example-card">
        <span class="proof-chip proof-chip--soft">Observed property example</span>
        <h3>{{ example.title }}</h3>
        <span class="example-metric">{{ example.value }}</span>
        <p>{{ example.summary }}</p>
        <div class="mini-note">{{ example.note }}</div>
      </article>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-intro">
      <span class="eyebrow">Fit</span>
      <h2>Best fit: premium Gulf Coast homes where the payout deserves close attention.</h2>
      <p><a href="/property-management/">Seascape property management</a> is built for owners who want revenue visibility, strong guest care, local follow-through, and plain-English owner updates. The best fit is a premium Gulf Coast home, especially in the $110k-$150k+ gross lane.</p>
      <div class="section-proof-rail">
        <span class="proof-chip proof-chip--soft">{{ benchmark.scopeLabel }}</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="fit-grid">
      <article class="fit-card">
        <span class="eyebrow">Best Fit</span>
        <ul class="quick-list">
          {% for bullet in fitBullets %}
          <li>{{ bullet }}</li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </article>
      <article class="fit-card">
        <span class="eyebrow">Fit boundary</span>
        <p>Homes projected below $110k gross may need a fee above 15% unless there is a strategic reason to approve the fit. Seascape's current fee structure is 10-15% at the company level, but this benchmark is not a blanket quote for every home.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-shell">
    <span class="eyebrow">Private teardown</span>
    <h2>Want the same scan on your home?</h2>
    <p>Send the listing URL, owner statement, fee quote, or property address. Seascape will run a short Revenue Teardown that shows what is already clear, what still deserves a closer look, and what you should ask before any switch conversation.</p>
    <a class="btn btn-gold cta-button" href="{{ ctaPath }}" data-track-event="owner_primary_cta_click" data-page-slug="owner-fee-revenue-leak-benchmark-2026">Request Your Revenue Teardown</a>
    <p class="cta-note">This page sends you into the shared teardown intake route. Missing statements, calendars, reviews, or fee terms stay marked unknown.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section method-mobile mobile-only">
    <div class="section-intro" style="margin-bottom:0">
      <span class="eyebrow">How To Read This Benchmark</span>
      <p>The benchmark uses Seascape's 5-home Gulf Coast operating data where observed, labels scenario math separately, and helps frame the owner conversation before a property-specific teardown.</p>
      <div class="section-proof-rail">
        <span class="proof-chip proof-chip--soft">{{ benchmark.scopeLabel }}</span>
        <span class="proof-chip proof-chip--soft">Scenario math, not a forecast</span>
        <span class="proof-chip proof-chip--soft">{{ benchmark.refreshedLabel }}</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>

<footer class="footer">© 2026 <a href="/">Seascape Vacations</a> · <a href="/property-management/">Property Management</a> · <a href="/property-management/vacation-rental-management-fees-florida/">Management Fees</a></footer>
</body>
</html>
